# Session Discipline

Always-on conduct. (The deployed-skill-cache guardrail is **Claude-surface only** —
it catches edits to a cloud-synced bundle *outside* this workspace, which Cursor
rules cannot see — so it is not mirrored here.)

## Session log (wrap-up)

At wrap-up, write a full reverse-chron entry only when the session made a real
judgment call: a choice among options, a scope/priority/risk decision, or a
measurement that resolves something open. Follow the living `docs/SESSIONS.md`
header — append-only, **link out** (never restate canonical values).
Use Focus / Shipped (branch+commit) / Decisions-defects (link the actual owner) /
Live-ops state where relevant. **Open / next** is optional historical context for
that session; do not copy the current queue into it or add a pointer-only stub when
the queue changes. The living header in `docs/SESSIONS.md` links to `STATE.md`, the
owner of current priorities and obligations. Mechanical output without a judgment
call, trivial turns and read-only turns need no full entry.
Grounding: `feedback_session_log_discipline` (owner
`docs/operational_rules.md §7`); bind:
[`Rule 7`](../../docs/operational_rules.md#7-one-canonical-owner-per-fact-every-other-mention-links-or-is-a-labeled-mirror).

## Fetch before a multi-step build

Before scaffolding, building out, or implementing a pipeline/stage/runner/harness,
run `git fetch origin && git log --oneline origin/main ^HEAD | head -20` and grep
for your target files. This repo runs from concurrent worktrees; a parallel
branch may already have landed the work (PR #325's PR-2 was mooted this way).
Reconcile before executing; re-fetch before pushing. Grounding:
`feedback_check_origin_main_before_multistep_build` +
`feedback_recent_gitlog_before_scaffolding_call`.

